# Real trade data and secrets - never committed
trading.db
*.xlsx
*.csv

# Screenshots/photos dropped in this folder are assumed to be personal
# (account screenshots, recovery codes, statements) - ignored by default
# so a stray `git add -A` can never publish one to the public repo.
# Add a specific `!filename.png` exception below if a project image ever
# genuinely needs committing.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# .streamlit holds real secrets, so the whole folder is ignored - the two
# exceptions below are the files that DO belong in Git: the example
# secrets file (no real values in it) and the app's theme, which has to
# be committed or the deployed app falls back to Streamlit's default look.
.streamlit/*
!.streamlit/secrets.toml.example
!.streamlit/config.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
